            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, thank you for referring this 69-year-old female patient who presented with acute lower abdominal pain and suspected tubal pregnancy. On admission, clinical examination, transvaginal ultrasound, and serum beta-hCG measurement confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy. Given the patient's hemodynamic stability, she was taken to the operating theatre, where laparoscopic salpingectomy was performed without complications. Histopathological examination confirmed the diagnosis. The postoperative course was uneventful. The patient was mobilized early and discharged in good general condition on the second postoperative day. We recommend follow-up monitoring of beta-hCG levels until normalization and gynecological review in four to six weeks. Please do not hesitate to contact us should any questions arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
